Status - Overview: render the Storage card as widgets when the Apex theme is
active

luci-theme-apex shows this Status card as widgets: one widget per mount (Disk
space, Temp space and every extra mount the stock card lists). A theme cannot
supply that markup hack-free: the card is rendered client-side by this include
(owned by luci-mod-status; a second copy in the theme package would be an apk
file conflict) from live ubus data (system.info and luci.getMountPoints), so
the markup has to come from here.

The theme in use is read on every render from L.env.media (set by the luci-base
header template), so switching themes needs no reboot and no reload logic:
  - Apex (/luci-static/apex): widgets (ax-sys-* / ax-mem-* classes, styled by the
    theme's cascade.css; one section per metric with an h4 title, a percentage,
    value / total and a role="meter"; all strings via _()).
  - any other theme, or when the data is missing: the stock table below,
    byte-identical to before (verified against the minified build; no extra request
    on that path - the ubus calls are the same).
Each widget shows used / free / total and the mount point with its device (the
data carries no filesystem type). The skip list of the stock card (/rom, /tmp,
/dev, /overlay, /) is kept for the extra mounts.

Applies to: https://git.openwrt.org/project/luci.git
            @ 350fc919675bb62e415927afff65697fcb8f775d (pinned in feeds.conf.default)
Applied by: tools/cw-apply-feed-patches.sh (patch -p1, zero fuzz - the build
            fails if upstream changes these lines; re-port it then).
Upstream status: not submitted (CleanWRT-specific).

